    {
      "id": "claim_e65a9dfd24434c30a111c38ae69afc1b",
      "statement": "wrap_model_call handlers are composed via _chain_model_call_handlers(): first handler wraps all others, creating an outer-to-inner execution chain. Each handler receives a handler callback that returns ModelResponse. Commands from each layer are accumulated (inner-first, then outer) into a list without merging, allowing outer middleware to control state updates. Async handlers compose similarly via _chain_async_model_call_handlers().",
      "evidence": [
